            <div xml:id="d965">

                <pb facs="0759" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/8321</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Parker, representing American interests, to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-28T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1916, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>622. Department’s 548, November 13, 4 p.m. Foreign Office reply yesterday states
                    War Department addressed military commandant Sonora to end that if there is no
                    objection the arms be returned to interested persons.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
